From ed31ea4b0280e063c393a10bff755700eb45e2dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "MR. ARX" <dev@nexeris.dev>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 16:14:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add HLS-based direct download fallback (Bunny MP4 rendition
 is currently broken)

- New /api/video/[id]/hls-download route: streams a downloadable file
  built live from the video's HLS segments (.m3u8 -> concatenated .ts),
  same auth/rate-limit/audit gates as the existing download route.
- Independent of Bunny Stream's per-resolution MP4 rendition feature,
  which is what's currently misbehaving (reported to Bunny support).
- VideoDownloadButton now calls this route instead.
- lib/bunny.ts: added buildHlsMasterUrl / hlsPullZoneConfigured, reusing
  the existing token-auth signing logic.

Known limitation: streams for the duration of the whole file, so very
long recordings may hit serverless execution time limits on some plans.
Revert to the MP4-rendition path once Bunny's issue is fixed.
---
 .env.example                             |  22 +++
 app/api/video/[id]/hls-download/route.ts | 179 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 components/VideoDownloadButton.tsx       |  33 ++---
 lib/bunny.ts                             |  23 +++
 4 files changed, 236 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 app/api/video/[id]/hls-download/route.ts

